THE DEFECT WAS ALREADY FIXED; THE TRACKER NEVER MOVED. Commit 7b45113 (2026-08-21)
states "Closed: BOB-079, BOB-158" in its own message, and the fix is present at HEAD.
The row still read Queued/Issues four days later — the §11.4.146(D3) status-custody
class running in the direction people forget: not a status outrunning its evidence,
but evidence outrunning its status. Both leave the tracker lying.

--- the mechanism at HEAD (tests/conftest.py:227) ---
_get_policy = getattr(asyncio.events, "_get_event_loop_policy", None)
with a documented version matrix in the surrounding comment:
  3.14.6   _get_event_loop_policy present; public getter WARNS
  3.12.13  _get_event_loop_policy ABSENT;  public getter is silent
Feature detection, not a version check — which is why it spans both.

